    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "comment-intro",
        "parent_id": null,
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# 🔀 Conditional Logic Engine\n\nRoutes one number to one of three outputs with If nodes. Use it to learn how a workflow branches, and how two If nodes chained on their false handles act as an else branch. No model runs.\n\n**How it works:** \"1️⃣ Input value\" (75) feeds two Code nodes. \"< 50?\" returns `value < 50` and \"> 100?\" returns `value > 100`. Each If node forwards its value on if_true when its condition is true, or on if_false otherwise, and emits nothing on the other handle. \"Low? (if_true)\" sends the low message to low_priority. \"High? (if_true)\" sends the high message to high_priority. The medium message passes two gates: \"Not low? (if_false)\" lets it through only when the value is not below 50, and \"Not high either? (if_false)\" only when it is not above 100. \"📋 Decision report\" lists both checks in \"Result\".\n\n**Try this:** Set \"1️⃣ Input value\" to 30, then 150. The message moves from medium_priority to low_priority, then to high_priority, and the other two outputs stay empty."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "selected": false,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 560,
          "height": 423,
          "selectable": true
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {},
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "type": "nodetool.text.Prompt",
        "data": {
          "prompt": "## Conditional Logic Decision Result\n\n**Input Value:** {{ value }}\n\n**Condition Checks:**\n- Less than 50? {{ lt_50 }}\n- Greater than 100? {{ gt_100 }}\n\nOnly one of low_priority, medium_priority and high_priority receives a message. An If node emits on one handle per run, so the branches that are not taken stay silent."
        },
